<onlyinclude>'''Boids''' is Craig Reynolds's computer model for simulating flocking-like motion using locally interacting virtual individuals. It was introduced in 1987 for computer animation.

== Explanation ==
Each simulated individual steers away from close neighbors, tends to align its movement with nearby individuals and moves toward the local group. Together these rules can create flock-like motion without a central leader. The simulation does not reproduce every feature of real bird behavior.

